 in winter. Come dressed for the cold even in summer. The lower slopes of Mount Etna are home to the renowned Val Demone Wine Region, where ancient lava soils nurture exceptional vineyards. Visitors can enjoy wine tastings, explore family-run wineries, and even stay overnight in scenic vineyard estates nestled beneath the mountain’s dramatic silhouette.","grounding":[{"source":"wikivoyage","title":"Mount Etna","url":"https://en.wikivoyage.org/wiki/Mount_Etna","licence":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}],"facts":{"population":619,"visit_h":5}},"highlights":[{"id":"hl-etna","name":"Etna","kind":"Peak","lat":37.75103,"lon":14.99403,"dist_km":0.4,"sig":2.997,"rank_score":13.86,"resolved_by":"catalogue","fact":"vulcano attivo italiano","image":{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ea/NAS_Sigonella_Backed_by_Mount_Etna_%286473839%29.jpg/500px-NAS_Sigonella_Backed_by_Mount_Etna_%286473839%29.jpg?utm_source=it.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","author":"U.S. Navy photo by Petty Officer 2nd Class Jacques-Laurent Jean-Gilles","licence":"Public domain","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:NAS_Sigonella_Backed_by_Mount_Etna_(6473839).jpg","ok_print":true},"wikipedia":"https://it.wikipedia.org/wiki/Etna","heritage":true},{"id":"hl-naxos","name":"Naxos","kind":"Museum","lat":37.82399,"lon":15.27398,"dist_km":25.7,"rank_score":7.86,"resolved_by":"catalogue","image":{"url":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/Special:FilePath/Walls%20at%20Naxos%2C%20Sicily%20%2871735239%29.jpg?width=960","author":"Alun Salt from Derby and Leicester, UK","licence":"CC BY-SA 2.0","licence_url":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/2.0","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Walls_at_Naxos,_Sicily_(71735239).jpg","w":2581,"h":1973,"ok_print":true}},{"id":"hl-acireale-cathedral","name":"Acireale Cathedral","kind":"Cathedral","lat":37.61305,"lon":15.16609,"dist_km":21.8,"rank_score":7.22,"resolved_by":"catalogue","image":{"url":"https://commons.wikimed